{'symbol': 'COP', 'date': '2022-11-22 16:15:00', 'title': 'SEMPRA ANNOUNCES STRATEGIC PARTNERSHIP WITH CONOCOPHILLIPS FOR PORT ARTHUR LNG', 'text': 'SAN DIEGO , NOV. 22, 2022 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- SEMPRA\xa0(NYSE: SRE) (BMV: SRE) TODAY ANNOUNCED THAT ITS SUBSIDIARY, SEMPRA INFRASTRUCTURE, AND CONOCOPHILLIPS (NYSE: COP) HAVE EXECUTED A 20-YEAR SALE AND PURCHASE AGREEMENT (SPA) FOR 5 MILLION TONNES PER ANNUM (MTPA) OF LIQUEFIED NATURAL GAS (LNG) FROM PHASE 1 OF THE PROPOSED PORT ARTHUR LNG PROJECT UNDER DEVELOPMENT IN JEFFERSON COUNTY, TEXAS. THE PARTIES HAVE ALSO ENTERED INTO AN EQUITY SALE AND PURCHASE AGREEMENT WHEREBY CONOCOPHILLIPS WILL ACQUIRE 30% OF THE EQUITY IN PHASE 1 OF PORT ARTHUR LNG, AND A NATURAL GAS SUPPLY MANAGEMENT AGREEMENT WHEREBY CONOCOPHILLIPS WILL MANAGE THE FEEDGAS SUPPLY REQUIREMENTS FOR PHASE 1 OF THE PROPOSED LIQUEFACTION FACILITY.'}